# Place these lines FIRST INSIDE the existing public
# *.hi5central.com { ... } site block, BEFORE all @managed* and @tenant*
# handle directives and BEFORE any file_server or reverse_proxy fallback.
# Do not add this matcher to the generic self-hosted Caddyfile.
#
# This regex reserves customer-qualified UAT/Test and all pilot-* hostnames.
# Explicit legacy uat.hi5central.com, test.hi5central.com, uat-api, test-api,
# test-rmm and test-admin remain outside the expression and continue routing.
#
# handle is required; a top-level "respond @unapprovedSandbox" is sorted
# AFTER the existing handle directives by the Caddyfile adapter.
# (?i) handles mixed-case Host values. The top-level HTTPS catchall (separate\n# snippet) returns 421 for trailing-dot hosts if wildcard site selection fails.\n# In CEL regexp strings use [.] instead of \. to avoid escape parsing errors.
@unapprovedSandbox expression {http.request.host}.matches('(?i)^(?:[a-z0-9-]+(?:uat|test)(?:-(?:api|portal|rmm|admin|downloads|connect|turn))?|pilot-[a-z0-9-]+)[.]hi5central[.]com[.]*
handle @unapprovedSandbox {
    respond "Not Found" 404
}
)
handle @unapprovedSandbox {
    respond "Not Found" 404
}
